  "provider_query": "Open the Chiphell viewthread page and record whether the body is a captcha shell",
  "answer": "**Result:** the classic Chiphell `viewthread` URL did **not** return a thread body. The fetch was empty (captcha-shell / no content). A pretty `thread-*-1-1.html` URL on the same site returned a real post page.\n\n1. **Direct open of `forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=2452882`** — body was **“No content found”** (one line). Not a thread; consistent with an empty challenge/captcha shell or a blocked fetch.  \n   Source: https://www.chiphell.com/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=2452882\n\n2. **Indexed `viewthread` pages (tids 2452882, 2461781, 2541412)** — snippets are the **forum homepage** (announcements, section lists, today’s stats), not post text. The viewthread query is not delivering the thread body to the crawler.  \n   Sources: [web:2], [web:4], [web:5]\n\n3. **Pretty URL `thread-2462208-1-1.html`** — **not** a captcha shell. Full thread body: title, view/reply counts, posts #1–#16, reply form, footer (“Processed in … Gzip On, Redis On”). Topic is a user complaint about captcha UX, not a site challenge page.  \n   Source: https://www.chiphell.com/thread-2462208-1-1.html [web:17]\n\n4. **Same thread in search** — matches the live page (posts about curve captchas, reCAPTCHA, cookies). Confirms the pretty URL is real content.  \n   Source: [web:8]\n\n5. **Related login-captcha thread** (`thread-2522672-1-1.html`) — also real posts (cookie/AdGuard login issues), not a shell.  \n   Source: [web:9]\n\n6. **Security-policy thread** (`thread-2844250-1-1.html`) — real posts about “请求已被站点的安全策略拦截,” not a captcha page itself.  \n   Source: [web:11]\n\n7. **Forum list pages** (`forumdisplay`, `forum-146-*.html`) — normal board listings, not viewthread and not captcha shells.  \n   Sources: [web:0], [web:3], [web:6]\n\n8. **Homepage** — normal CHH index (reviews, sections).  \n   Source: [web:7]\n\n**Record:** `mod=viewthread` → empty / non-thread body (captcha shell or equivalent block). `thread-{tid}-1-1.html` → actual thread HTML.",
